<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7809"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Taken from the Witchita Cold Cases Web Page: <BR> <BR>&#34;Sept. 14,  1988: The body  of Michael J. Fowler was found in rural northeast  Sedgwick County.   Investigators believe Mr. Fowler was murdered at an  unknown location  then transported to where his body was found at 85th  Street North and  Oliver in Sedgwick County, Kansas.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7809-->
<!--Post: 7858--><!--Time: 1108714707-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7858"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 12:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wrote about this in another thread, about the initials of the last names of BTK&#39;s victims spelling the word F_OW_R, if we give Vian the name on her headstone, Relford. <BR> <BR>That is F for Fox, O for Otero, W for Wegerle or Williams, and R for Relford. <BR> <BR>So, this could be interpreted as BTK wanting to spell the word &#34;FLOWER&#34; or &#34;FOWLER&#34;. <BR> <BR>In order for that theory to be true, Wegerle or Williams should have a maiden name starting with either L or E. I don&#39;t know their maiden names. <BR> <BR>Then there is still a victim out there, not known, whose last name would start with either L or E. <BR> <BR>If the theory is correct, BTK must&#39;ve had it for Mr. Fowlerm or his family, and was spelling his family name until he finished spelling it, then he went for him. <BR> <BR>Okay, just a theory. <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7858-->
<!--Post: 9490--><!--Time: 1109538814-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9490"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This case needs to be looked at ... Is there any other information on it?   <BR> <BR>Ztar- Looks like you were wrong here, but it was a good theory.  I just don&#39;t know where Hedge and Davis would fit in.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9490-->
<!--Post: 9894--><!--Time: 1109695311-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 8:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->V- I think Mike Fowler at the time was a Park City police officer. Did he stumble onto BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9894-->
<!--Post: 10271--><!--Time: 1109869149-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10271"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 8:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You serious? Was Mike Fowler a Park City police officer?  <BR> <BR>Verm, maybe he was trying to spell something else after flower or Fowler?  <BR> <BR>So far he is said to have confessed to only six of the murders... which of the known eight is he leaving out? I understand the Bright murder, he may not claim that one, but which other? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10271-->
<!--Post: 10274--><!--Time: 1109871688-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10274"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 9:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/cold_cases/fowler.html" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/c old_cases/fowler.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10274-->
<!--Post: 10370--><!--Time: 1109916592-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10370"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->V- I just went there to post what you just did! Wow, that&#39;s scary.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10370-->
<!--Post: 10373--><!--Time: 1109917010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->V-I knew Mikey! His big sister and I used to hang out a lot when we were teenagers! Wait a minute - Maybe it was his brother that was on the police force! Can you see where this would fit into E&#39;s timeline? Z - did you find Fowler in that puzzle?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10373-->
<!--Post: 10644--><!--Time: 1110075476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1988&#42; <BR>1/??: Mrs. Phillip &#40;Mary&#41; Fager receives letter from BTK which admires the Fager mass-murder, but denies responsibility <BR>- 9/14: Michael J. Fowler &#40;Sedgwick County, KS&#41;; c.o.d. unspecified, body dumped in rural area <BR>already there lol<!--/Text--></td></tr>
